  "commentary": "Specialization of a rank 17 fibration of the known K3 surface of discriminant 1152. Discovered by Noam Elkies, Zev Klagsbrun, and Samuel Li.\r\n\r\nSpecialization at T = -2868768/362209 of the elliptic fibration of X1152 given by:\r\ny^2 + (Lx+B)y = x(x+D)(x+E),\r\nwhere\r\nB = pE + qD + pq(L-p-q),\r\nL = 466548T^2 - 828066T + 32416,\r\np = -478380T^2 - 1076788T + 103008,\r\nq = 82612T^2 - 180205T + 81622,\r\nD = -26666192028T^4 - 91335649060T^3 + 11566653808T^2 + 239872553168T - 53374213248,\r\nE = -47423161625T^4 + 118525002574T^3 - 104259187849T^2 + 76235905664T - 24372268764.\r\n\r\nUpper bound (16 Oct 2026, S. Hackfort): r_an = 32 subject to GRH. Explicit-formula bound with a per-curve optimised test function (radix-rank), L = 12.41, all 2,529,822,599 primes p < 6.02e10, certified with Arb: [33.99820448 +/- 1.83e-9] < 34; root number +1. With the 32 independent points the rank is exactly 32 subject to GRH and BSD. Certificates and code: https://github.com/sectio-aurea-q/radix-rank/blob/main/highrank/record_4239.md",
